From: Soe Thura <6492082+thixpin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:25:31 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Translate lhbrx and dcbst

Forza Motorsport 4 uses lhbrx and dcbst once each; the recompiler translates neither. lhbrx
loads a byte-reversed halfword, zero-extended, as lwbrx does for words. dcbst only writes a cache
block back to memory, which the host keeps coherent, so like dcbf it emits nothing.
---
 XenonRecomp/recompiler.cpp | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/XenonRecomp/recompiler.cpp b/XenonRecomp/recompiler.cpp
index 35d6db0..a976752 100644
--- a/XenonRecomp/recompiler.cpp
+++ b/XenonRecomp/recompiler.cpp
@@ -946,6 +946,10 @@ bool Recompiler::Recompile(
         // no op
         break;
 
+    case PPC_INST_DCBST:
+        // no op: like dcbf it only writes the block back to memory, which the host keeps coherent
+        break;
+
     case PPC_INST_DCBT:
         // no op
         break;
@@ -1345,6 +1349,14 @@ bool Recompiler::Recompile(
         println("{}.u32));", r(insn.operands[2]));
         break;
 
+    case PPC_INST_LHBRX:
+        // the halfword at (rA|0) + (rB), byte-reversed, zero-extended
+        print("\t{}.u64 = __builtin_bswap16(PPC_LOAD_U16(", r(insn.operands[0]));
+        if (insn.operands[1] != 0)
+            print("{}.u32 + ", r(insn.operands[1]));
+        println("{}.u32));", r(insn.operands[2]));
+        break;
+
     case PPC_INST_LWBRX:
         print("\t{}.u64 = __builtin_bswap32(PPC_LOAD_U32(", r(insn.operands[0]));
         if (insn.operands[1] != 0)
